-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of X_H(q²M')→ X₀(M') off j=0,1728
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), where $H=$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction of units $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $K_0$ be the corresponding $L$-subfield attached to the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, and assume $K_0\le K$. Let $j\in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ` of the modular invariant. Let $P$ be a place of $K$ over $L$ (a proper valuation subring of $K$ containing $L$ whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring), and suppose $\operatorname{ord}_P j = 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_P (j-1728)=0$. Then the ramification index of $P$ along the inclusion $K_0\hookrightarrow K$ — the least positive $n$ of the form $\operatorname{ord}_P f$ with $0\ne f\in K_0$ — equals $1$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the statement that the covering $X(\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))\to X_0(M')$ is unramified at every non-cuspidal point whose $j$-invariant differs from $0$ and $1728$, the elliptic points and cusps being the only places where the stabiliser in $\Gamma_0(M')/\{\pm 1\}$ is nontrivial. It feeds the unramifiedness results for the full-level tower at height-one primes away from the cusps and the two elliptic $j$-values.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_ramificationIndexAlong_inclusion_eq_one_of_ord_eq_zero_of_ord_sub_eq_zero_xH_levelH.lean

